           merely handed, and this rule is the only defence for a NON-compound command,
           which allow-compound-bash.sh never sees.
           The everyday pipeline is not lost: `… | xargs wc -l` is compound, so the hook
           resolves xargs to the command it will exec and judges that instead. Bare
           `xargs …` now prompts. */}}
